# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore — suppressed findings
# =============================================================================
# Two entries, both at the bottom of this file. Read the rule before adding a
# third.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE RULE FOR ADDING ANYTHING HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An ignore file is where security debt goes to be forgotten. Every entry must
# carry three things, or it does not go in:
#
#   1. WHY it is not exploitable HERE — not "it is only a HIGH", but a concrete
#      reason this code path is unreachable or the impact does not apply.
#   2. WHO decided, and when.
#   3. An EXPIRY date. Trivy enforces it: past that date the finding comes back
#      and breaks the build again, which forces a re-review instead of a
#      permanent silent exception.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# Worked example of an acceptable entry:
#
#   # CVE-2025-0000 — glibc parser bug reachable only via setuid binaries.
#   # Our containers run as UID 1000/101 with capabilities: drop ALL and a
#   # read-only root filesystem, so there is no setuid path to reach it.
#   # No fixed version published upstream as of review.
#   # Reviewed: 2026-08-24. Re-check when Debian ships a patched glibc.
#   CVE-2025-0000 exp:2026-11-24
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - "the build is red and I need to merge"        -> fix it or revert
#   - a CVE with an available fixed version         -> bump the dependency
#   - anything without an expiry date               -> that is not a decision,
#                                                      it is an abdication
#
# Note the pipeline already passes `--ignore-unfixed`, so findings with no
# upstream fix do not gate the build in the first place. If something reaches
# this file, a fix existed and was consciously deferred.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EKS public API endpoint — terraform/eks.tf:64 and :79
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These two are the SAME decision, already argued in eks.tf:67-78. They did not
# appear before because the pipeline ran Trivy 0.28, which did not carry these
# checks; Trivy 0.70 does. The configuration did not change — the scanner did.
#
# WHY it is accepted here:
#   The endpoint is public but NOT unauthenticated. Reaching it still requires
#   a valid IAM principal mapped to an EKS access entry, over TLS. What is
#   exposed is the ability to attempt authentication, not the cluster.
#
#   It also cannot simply be turned off. The `deploy` job runs on
#   GitHub-hosted runners, which reach the API server over the internet. With
#   endpoint_public_access = false, CD stops working entirely unless a
#   self-hosted runner is placed inside the VPC. Narrowing public_access_cidrs
#   is the better fix, but GitHub's runner ranges are hundreds of rotating
#   CIDRs against an EKS limit of 40, so that is not a drop-in change either.
#
#   Compensating controls already in place: IAM + OIDC authentication, the CD
#   role scoped to one namespace (asserted on every run by the "Confirm
#   least-privilege scoping" step), and control-plane audit logging to
#   CloudWatch — so an attempt against this endpoint is recorded.
#
# WHO/WHEN: dollarsmoney, 2026-09-13.
#
# WHAT WOULD RETIRE THESE: a self-hosted runner in the VPC, or a stable egress
# IP (NAT/VPN) to put in public_access_cidrs. Either makes both entries
# unnecessary — delete them, do not extend them.
#
# The expiry is the point: in six months this comes back and breaks the build
# again, forcing this argument to be made once more rather than inherited.
AWS-0040 exp:2027-03-13
AWS-0041 exp:2027-03-13
